# ─── Google Apps Script deployment ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These values are NOT stored in version control. Copy this file to .env.local
# for reference; the actual values live in two places:
#
#   .clasp.json          — created by `npm run setup` or `clasp clone`
#   Script Properties    — set via the GAS editor:
#                          Project Settings → Script Properties → Add property
#
# ─── .clasp.json (local only, gitignored) ─────────────────────────────────────
#
#   scriptId   — the Apps Script project ID
#                  e.g. 1z_J4gESMkKVbiw8tPqlQkkrF_PKzkatNJrrXHS7ORvMqBnd-UDPtLMSR
#
#   parentId   — the Google Drive file ID of the bound/container spreadsheet
#                  e.g. 1D_tPksBpflSUD2Hx4I_MYHPQL2yYz_V-c-1uVkkaaIo
#
# ─── Script Properties (set in GAS editor, never in code) ─────────────────────
#
# AUTH_SPREADSHEET_ID
#   Spreadsheet ID of the auth workbook ("Inventory Auth (do not share)").
#   Auto-created and stored on first login if absent — you do not need to
#   set this manually unless you are migrating to an existing auth workbook.
#
# SOURCE_SPREADSHEET_ID
#   Spreadsheet ID of the "Product Info" source sheet used by the ONE-TIME
#   migration script (seedFromInventorySheet). Only needed before running
#   the migration. Example: 1D_tPksBpflSUD2Hx4I_MYHPQL2yYz_V-c-1uVkkaaIo
#
# SOURCE_SHEET_GID
#   The gid (numeric tab ID) of the specific sheet within SOURCE_SPREADSHEET_ID.
#   Find it in the URL: ...#gid=1625801440
#   Example: 1625801440
#
# ─── How to set Script Properties ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   1. Open the GAS editor:  npm run open
#   2. Project Settings (gear icon) → Script Properties
#   3. Add each key/value pair listed above
#
# ─── Local development ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   No environment variables are needed for `npm run dev`. The local mock
#   (src/client/lib/serverMock.ts) runs entirely in the browser with seed
#   data from src/mock/seed.json — no GAS connection required.
